														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2707733">
									

<p>Generally good, but I have a couple of nits to pick:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>waves reaching up to and over a peak height of 25 metres</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Sorry, this is one of my major pet peeves. Literally every number is either up to or over 25, so this really doesn't tell us anything at all. I would say, &quot;waves typically/frequently/occasionally reaching a peak height of 25 metres,&quot; depending on how often you envision this happening. The sentence about outliers already tells us that the waves can reach greater heights.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This is believed to be a form of mind-affecting anomaly, evidenced by any person coming into contact or close proximity with SCP-2467 for an extended period of time (3-10 days depending on the individual) comes to believe the SCP-2467 is correct in its actions, and will attempt to aid it however they are able.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>As Buttfranklin said, this is just ungrammatical. It could possibly work if you changed it to, &quot;evidenced by <strong>the fact that</strong> any person, etc.&quot; You'd probably be better off splitting it into two or three sentences, though.</p>

							</div>

								
					
